@@ -32,6 +32,13 @@ best-effort per source: one damaged settings file is reported without blocking h
 initial sync. The final token/config swap is serialized behind any active sync, so an older request
 cannot restore superseded authorization.
 
+If the server reports that this installation authorization was revoked (including account deletion),
+`connect` removes the stale local authorization, pending automatic state, and owned hooks through the
+normal lifecycle cleanup, then starts a fresh pairing without requiring an abandoned pairing, changing
+the installation identity, or changing local source definitions. Partial auxiliary cleanup is reported as a warning. Other reconciliation
+errors, including transient network failures, leave the existing connection in place and do not start
+a replacement pairing.
+
